{"entries":[{"caption":"Seasonal variation in community-level bat acoustic activity across eight sites in the northern Sierra Nevada, California, April–October 2015. (a) Total seasonal pattern from the day-of-year model, shown as the posterior distribution of the equal-site averaged expected number of 5-min intervals per night in which a bat call occurred. (b) Conditional seasonal pattern from the environmental model after accounting for nightly mean temperature, relative humidity, and lunar phase; the curve is likewise averaged equally across sites. (c) Site-specific seasonal phenology from the total seasonal model. Thin gray lines show posterior median trajectories for individual sites; the black line and shaded bands show the equal-site averaged seasonal trajectory. In panels a and b, and for the average in panel c, lines indicate posterior medians and shaded bands indicate 50%, 80%, and 89% credible intervals from darkest to lightest.","key":"fig-seasonality","order":{"number":1,"section":[1,3,0,0,0,0,0]}}],"headings":["results","sampling-and-acoustic-activity","model-development-and-adequacy","seasonal-activity","conditional-environmental-responses","temperature","relative-humidity","lunar-phase","echolocation-frequency-groups","frequency-dependent-humidity-responses","frequency-dependent-temperature-responses","frequency-specific-seasonal-phenology","lunar-responses-among-frequency-groups","summary-of-principal-findings","tables-and-figures-to-generate"]}